# Phase 5 SUBMIT-CARD-PREVIEW (fx v0.0.16's 70611a91): five lines typed (a
# line feed, Ctrl-J, between them) and their Enter in one write (`key -H`,
# one tmux send-keys), on the screen p5-transcript-submit fills -- no frame
# shows the five-row composer before the Enter is read. (A paste and an
# Enter in one read is refused on both: `Paste was not applied because extra
# input followed its end marker`.) Where fx measures the preview's room from the last
# committed frame (the one-row composer's), the frame that clears the
# composer shows what that frame left room for. The wires on both sides of
# the write, the turn held at its first chunk.
gateway p5-submit-preview-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
wait 4
type fill the screen
wait 1
key Enter
wait 8
snap filled
wire oneread-before
key -H 6f 6e 65 72 65 61 64 20 6c 69 6e 65 20 31 0a 6f 6e 65 72 65 61 64 20 6c 69 6e 65 20 32 0a 6f 6e 65 72 65 61 64 20 6c 69 6e 65 20 33 0a 6f 6e 65 72 65 61 64 20 6c 69 6e 65 20 34 0a 6f 6e 65 72 65 61 64 20 6c 69 6e 65 20 35 0d
held
wait 1
snap oneread-held
release
wait 3
snap oneread
wire oneread-after
gwlog
